  "title": "# Build: profile-manager (Current profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): a plugin to manage build prof…",
  "asked": "# Build: profile-manager (Current profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): a plugin to manage build profiles: view, browse, create, edit, delete, everything. Assigned agent: **Landin' Lenny** (book on his card; if busy and the all-rounder router is on main, whoever is free - record who). Register in the **current** profile (id `profile-manager`) + banner entry. (Profile `current` was just created; if it's missing, create it: `node framework/cli/profiles.mjs create \"Current\" --id current --select`.) ## Build on what exists - don't duplicate The console already has the **Build profiles** plugin (`build-profiles`: dialog + settings tab, banner chip, switch/create/rename/remove) over `framework/cli/profiles.mjs` (build-profiles@1) and the builds store. Grow THAT plugin into a full manager page (rename the plugin title to 'Build profiles' manager if needed; keep its id, data and every existing feature). ## Features - **Browse:** framework grid of every profile (collapsible rows): name, id, active star, description, counts (builds running / pending / complete / archived, pending items, queue steps), cost spent + cost left, last activity, created; sort/search/filter. Expand a row: its builds (with agent avatars once crew-live lands), pending list, queue, plan summary, files (`profiles.mjs where`). - **View** a profile page: all its builds and steps, timeline, totals, links to Builds page views filtered to it. - **Create** (name, id, description, copy from another profile, catalog on/off, make active), **Edit** (name, description, catalog, colour/icon for the banner chip), **Switch** (one tap; banner chip + context menu), **Duplicate**, **Merge** two profiles, **Move builds** between profiles (multi-select, drag rows onto a profile), **Archive / hide**, **Delete** = take off the list (data kept, restorable) with confirm; a separate 'Delete data too' that is owner-only and irreversible-confirm. Base profile and active profile can't be deleted. - **Cleanup helper:** flag archived builds that are actually complete (reconciler) - e.g. angel, big-dog, breakroom, refactor - with a one-tap fix. - Context-menu hooks everywhere: 'Build profiles...' and 'Move to profile' on any build row. - Commands declared once -> REST + MCP + CLI (list, get, create, update, select, duplicate, merge, move-builds, archive, remove, restore) so Amber can manage profiles by voice (reads ALLOW policy, changes veto, data delete confirm). - Tests, phone + desktop screenshots, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/profile-manager.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
